  "theorem": "Both targets are invertible and have positive marginal sign gaps, yet their Bloch columns are parallel and the two-column target has rank one. For every unit Bloch vector u perpendicular to z, X=(3z+4u)/5 and Z=(4z-3u)/5 are Hermitian involutions with XZ+ZX=0. Every member attains the same global Procrustes value because the target overlap is sqrt((3/5)^2+(4/5)^2)=1. The circle of u therefore gives infinitely many global minimizers. Two positive marginal gaps alone do not imply joint Clifford uniqueness; full two-column rank is essential in the qubit theorem."
